# Hf - Ugur interatomic potential, hard truncation, with the angular factor
#
# pair_style ugur/ang
# pair_coeff * * Hf.ugur.ang Hf
#
# Truncation: hard - phi2 does not vanish at rcut2, it stops at -266 meV (10.4 of k_B T at 296 K).  USE for static properties and for lattice dynamics: measured against neutron dispersion the hard sets average 9.5 % over the 29 elements that have one, against 12.7 % for the switched sets, and are closer in 23 of them.  DO NOT use for molecular dynamics: copper, whose step is 8.4 meV, drifts 350 meV/atom/ns in NVE and climbs from 296 K to over 1100 K in 200 ps
# MD: DO NOT USE.  At 600 K the crystal collapses: it reaches 441 K and its potential energy falls below the static lattice.  Static properties from this set are still valid.
#
# Lattice stability: screened on the 8^3 and 9^3 meshes AND along the
# symmetry path; no imaginary modes.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Hf at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
Hf Hf Hf 10.979555424603618 0.53662675026303175 0.19644879180139341 4.2275789315783365 8.5334140051489395e-07 -0.14995258010604762 0.019703183680140186 8.2940000000000005 4.6880419031516301 -1 -0.41872265001918596 0.90440920565087546
